    "https://westfield.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204936": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work - 1 Year Temporary, Benefited",
      "description": "Westfield State University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Social Work - 1 Year Temporary, Benefited Westfield State University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Social Work - 1 Year Temporary, Benefited Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Social Work - 1 Year Temporary, Benefited Category: Faculty/Librarians Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SOCIAL WORK Locations: Westfield, MA Posted: Sep 17, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $68,000.00 - $68,000.00 Position ID: 204936 Share About Westfield State University: In 1839, Westfield State University was founded on the ideals of Horace Mann who sought to improve society through education. We were the first public education institution without barrier to race, gender or economic class. The spirit of innovative thinking and social responsibility is forged in a curriculum of liberal arts and professional studies contributing to the development of knowledge, skills, and character essential for students to become responsible leaders and engaged citizens. Westfield State is a highly residential campus with approximately 55% of our 3,100 full-time undergraduate students living on campus. The campus is ideally situated on the edge of the Berkshire Mountains in western Massachusetts just 30 minutes from the thriving cultural centers of Springfield, Northampton, and Amherst with a selection of museums, theater, collegiate and minor league sports, hiking trails, and restaurants. The University is within 1.5 hours of Boston and Albany and within 3 hours of New York City and the Green Mountain range of Vermont. Thank You for Your Interest in Becoming a Westfield State Community Member You are welcome here. You can advance your career and make a difference here. We invite you to bring your whole self and talents to Westfield State University. The University seeks applicants whose record of teaching, student advising, research, and administration positions them to contribute to the everyday practice of our institutional values. Our Values Westfield State commits to values that strengthen a common bond among all members of our community and promotes a rich campus environment. Embrace Diversity - We treat all members of our community with dignity and respect. Maintain Excellence and Integrity - We maintain excellence and integrity in all that we do. Collaborate with Each Other - We make decisions in a transparent and collaborative manner. Provide Accessible Education - We commit to providing an accessible, affordable public higher education for all. Build a Strong Community - We are inclusive and ensure equity, supporting the personal development of all community members, and embracing multiple perspectives. Engage the Outside Community - We support civic engagement in local, regional, and global initiatives. Job Description: Campus Title: Assistant Professor State Job Title: Assistant Professor Department: Social Work Job Code: HA3200 FLSA Status: Exempt Funding: 7107-0029 Bargaining Unit: MSCA Job Type: Full-Time Temporary, Benefited Timeframe: Academic Year Shift: Monday-Friday, 8:30 am to 4:00 pm Regular Days Off: Saturday and Sunday Supervision Received: Reports directly to the chair of the Social Work Department Supervision Exercised: None Salary: $68,000 (salary may commensurate to coincide with education and experience) *Two positions will be hired off this posting* Position Description: Westfield State University Department of Social Work is seeking applications for a full-time, one-year contract Assistant Professor of Social Work. The responsibilities for the position will include teaching Social Work at the graduate level and undergraduate level in the University's existing BSW and MSW programs. The program is looking for faculty with the ability to teach clinical practice and foundation MSW and BSW classes. The position includes a 24-credit teaching load annually, student advising, scholarship (work toward a doctoral degree is considered scholarship), and service to the University. The position will start September 1, 2027. Requirements: Required Qualifications: MSW A minimum of two years post-masters direct practice experience A DSW or PhD in Social Work or Social Welfare is preferred (ABD will be considered) Additional Information: Salary: Salaries for current Westfield State University employees and individuals currently working for the state of Massachusetts must be calculated individually in accordance with collective bargaining agreements as well as state policies. State job specifications may be found on the Department of Higher Education's webpage . Employee Benefits: Benefits are an important component of an employee's total compensation package. Health Insurance: Westfield State offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: the MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Additional information regarding employee benefits is available on the University's Benefits & Wellness webpage . Disability Accommodations Westfield State University is committed to the full inclusion of individuals with disabilities and will ensure the availability of reasonable accommodations. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at (413) 572-8809 or visit us in the Horace Mann Building, 1st floor. Background Check Employment is contingent upon the successful completion and review of a background check. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify an applicant from consideration. Application Instructions: An online application is required. A complete application includes: Cover Letter* Curriculum vitae Unofficial copy of transcripts of highest degree Statement of teaching philosophy with areas for continuing scholarship Contact information for three reference letter providers** Notes: * In your cover letter please include the ways in which you would advance diversity and inclusion in your classroom and at the University. ** Contact information for three reference letter providers should be completed on the reference form. Applicants that are using Interfolio for an existing confidential letter of recommendation should provide the Interfolio based email address (e.g. ref1@interfolio.com). Application deadline: Review of applications will begin immediately. The job will remain open until finalists have been selected. NOTE: If you need assistance completing your application please contact our online Help Desk . The link to the help desk can be found at the top of the page via Contact Us. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Westfield State University 577 Western Avenue, Westfield,  MA  01086"
    },
    "https://westfield.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204930": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work / Tenure Track",
      "description": "Westfield State University\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work / Tenure Track Westfield State University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work / Tenure Track Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work / Tenure Track Category: Faculty/Librarians Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SOCIAL WORK Locations: Westfield, MA Posted: Sep 17, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $70,000.00 - $70,000.00 Position ID: 204930 Share About Westfield State University: In 1839, Westfield State University was founded on the ideals of Horace Mann who sought to improve society through education. We were the first public education institution without barrier to race, gender or economic class. The spirit of innovative thinking and social responsibility is forged in a curriculum of liberal arts and professional studies contributing to the development of knowledge, skills, and character essential for students to become responsible leaders and engaged citizens. Westfield State is a highly residential campus with approximately 55% of our 3,100 full-time undergraduate students living on campus. The campus is ideally situated on the edge of the Berkshire Mountains in western Massachusetts just 30 minutes from the thriving cultural centers of Springfield, Northampton, and Amherst with a selection of museums, theater, collegiate and minor league sports, hiking trails, and restaurants. The University is within 1.5 hours of Boston and Albany and within 3 hours of New York City and the Green Mountain range of Vermont. Thank You for Your Interest in Becoming a Westfield State Community Member You are welcome here. You can advance your career and make a difference here. We invite you to bring your whole self and talents to Westfield State University. The University seeks applicants whose record of teaching, student advising, research, and administration positions them to contribute to the everyday practice of our institutional values. Our Values Westfield State commits to values that strengthen a common bond among all members of our community and promotes a rich campus environment. Embrace Diversity - We treat all members of our community with dignity and respect. Maintain Excellence and Integrity - We maintain excellence and integrity in all that we do. Collaborate with Each Other - We make decisions in a transparent and collaborative manner. Provide Accessible Education - We commit to providing an accessible, affordable public higher education for all. Build a Strong Community - We are inclusive and ensure equity, supporting the personal development of all community members, and embracing multiple perspectives. Engage the Outside Community - We support civic engagement in local, regional, and global initiatives. Job Description: Campus Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Social Work / Tenure Track State Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor Department: Social Work Job Code: HA3200/HA3100 FLSA Status: Exempt Funding: 7107-0029 Bargaining Unit: MSCA Job Type: Full-Time, Permanent Timeframe: Academic Year Shift: Regular Course Schedule Regular Days Off: Saturday and Sunday Supervision Received: Reports directly to the chair of the Social Work Department Supervision Exercised: None Salary: $70,000 Annually (salary may commensurate to coincide with education and experience) *Two positions will be hired from this posting* General Statement of Duties: Program Description: The Department of Social Work at Westfield State University is seeking applications for: Multiple full-time tenure-track positions at the Assistant and Associate Rank to begin September 2027. Westfield State University's Master of Social Work Program is accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) with a single concentration in clinical practice. The MSW Program provides a clinically focused social work education using a hybrid model. Courses are offered two nights per week, with 2/3 of content delivered online and 1/3 delivered face-to-face. Significant office presence is required for meetings, advising, and general collaboration. Professors are required to teach both online and in-person; this is an office-based position. Beginning in 2022, the MSW Program offers a fully online degree path. In this model, classes are held synchronously on Zoom two nights per week and asynchronous work during the rest of the week. The BSW Program provides generalist social work education using a hybrid model. With 1/2 of content delivered online and 1/2 delivered face-to-face, all practice courses are 100% face-to-face. Classes are scheduled primarily between 8:00AM - 4:00PM, although a small percentage of classes are held online in the evenings. Responsibilities: Tenure-Track Assistant and Associate Professor The tenure track position will primarily teach across the BSW and MSW programs, both online and in-person. Teaching load will be 24 credits per year (12 credits per semester), additional responsibilities include: student advising; scholarship (including, where applicable, work toward a doctoral degree); and service to the university and wider community. Applicants will have the ability to teach online, and specific curricular areas of need include: Generalist Practice and Advanced Clinical Practice. Requirements: Qualifications: At the Assistant Professor Rank: Education MSW required with a minimum of two years post-master' s direct practice PhD in Social Work or Social Welfare (ABD will be considered at the Assistant rank) Licensure LICSW or LCSW (or state equivalent) required Teaching Experience Some college-level teaching preferred, including teaching assistantships or guest lecturing Practice Experience 2+ years of post-MSW direct practice experience Scholarship Evidence of scholarly potential: this can include dissertation research, publications, conference presentations Active research agenda is expected At the Associate Professor Rank: Education Master of Social Work (MSW) is required PhD in Social Work or Social Welfare Licensure LICSW (or state equivalent) is required Teaching Experience Five years of prior college-level teaching experience Experience teaching core social work courses Practice Experience Meaningful direct practice experience in social work (typically 2+ years post-MSW) Expertise in child/family welfare and child/family mental health Scholarship A demonstrated record of peer-reviewed publications and presentations Active research agenda or scholarly work in progress Service Evidence of professional service - field liaison work, committee involvement, community engagement Field education supervision experience is valued Other Common Expectations Knowledge of CSWE Educational Policy and Accreditation Standards (EPAS) Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in pedagogy Experience with field education coordination or supervision Additional Information: Salary: Salaries for current Westfield State University employees and individuals currently working for the state of Massachusetts must be calculated individually in accordance with collective bargaining agreements as well as state policies. State job specifications may be found on the Department of Higher Education's webpage . Employee Benefits: Benefits are an important component of an employee's total compensation package. Health Insurance: Westfield State offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: the MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Additional information regarding employee benefits is available on the University's Benefits & Wellness webpage . Disability Accommodations Westfield State University is committed to the full inclusion of individuals with disabilities and will ensure the availability of reasonable accommodations. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at (413) 572-8809 or visit us in the Horace Mann Building, 1st floor. Background Check Employment is contingent upon the successful completion and review of a background check. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify an applicant from consideration. Application Instructions: An online application is required. A complete application includes: Cover Letter* Curriculum vitae Unofficial copy of transcripts of highest degree Statement of teaching philosophy with areas for continuing scholarship Contact information for three reference letter providers** Notes: * In your cover letter please include the ways in which you would advance diversity and inclusion in your classroom and at the University. ** Contact information for three reference letter providers should be completed on the reference form. Applicants that are using Interfolio for an existing confidential letter of recommendation should provide the Interfolio based email address (e.g. ref1@interfolio.com). Application deadline: The search for this position will begin immediately and remain open until filled. NOTE: If you need assistance completing your application please contact our online Help Desk . The link to the help desk can be found at the top of the page via Contact Us. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Westfield State University 577 Western Avenue, Westfield,  MA  01086"
