    "https://westfield.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204408": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement Communications and Publications",
      "description": "Westfield State University\nJob Posting: Director of Advancement Communications and Publications Westfield State University \n\tJob Posting: Director of Advancement Communications and Publications Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Advancement Communications and Publications Category: Professional/Executive Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: INSTITUTIONAL ADVANCEMENT Locations: Westfield, MA Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $95,000.00 - $100,000.00 Position ID: 204408 Share About Westfield State University: In 1839, Westfield State University was founded on the ideals of Horace Mann who sought to improve society through education. We were the first public education institution without barrier to race, gender or economic class. The spirit of innovative thinking and social responsibility is forged in a curriculum of liberal arts and professional studies contributing to the development of knowledge, skills, and character essential for students to become responsible leaders and engaged citizens. Westfield State is a highly residential campus with approximately 55% of our 3,100 full-time undergraduate students living on campus. The campus is ideally situated on the edge of the Berkshire Mountains in western Massachusetts just 30 minutes from the thriving cultural centers of Springfield, Northampton, and Amherst with a selection of museums, theater, collegiate and minor league sports, hiking trails, and restaurants. The University is within 1.5 hours of Boston and Albany and within 3 hours of New York City and the Green Mountain range of Vermont. Thank You for Your Interest in Becoming a Westfield State Community Member You are welcome here. You can advance your career and make a difference here. We invite you to bring your whole self and talents to Westfield State University. The University seeks applicants whose record of teaching, student advising, research, and administration positions them to contribute to the everyday practice of our institutional values. Our Values Westfield State commits to values that strengthen a common bond among all members of our community and promotes a rich campus environment. Embrace Diversity - We treat all members of our community with dignity and respect. Maintain Excellence and Integrity - We maintain excellence and integrity in all that we do. Collaborate with Each Other - We make decisions in a transparent and collaborative manner. Provide Accessible Education - We commit to providing an accessible, affordable public higher education for all. Build a Strong Community - We are inclusive and ensure equity, supporting the personal development of all community members, and embracing multiple perspectives. Engage the Outside Community - We support civic engagement in local, regional, and global initiatives. Job Description: Campus Title: Director of Advancement Communications and Publications State Job Title: Director Department: Institutional Advancement Job Code: HA6000 FLSA Status: Exempt Funding: 7115-6014 Bargaining Unit: APA Job Type: Full-Time Permanent Timeframe: 52 Weeks Shift: Monday-Friday, 9am to 5pm Regular Days Off: Saturday and Sunday Salary: $95,000-$100,000 Annually (salary commensurate with education and experience) This is a fully in-person position at Westfield State University, with all duties performed on campus during the employee's regularly scheduled work hours to support direct engagement with students, colleagues, and the campus community, unless your position requires travel to perform said duties. General Statement of Duties: The Director is responsible for managing the day-to-day functions of Westfield State's growing communications program by planning, supporting, and executing communications to support the donor cultivation process for a comprehensive campaign and general Institutional Advancement friend and fundraising efforts. In addition, the position oversees the redevelopment of publications and print and digital communications in support of WSU, the WSU Foundation, Inc., and the WSU Alumni Association. With guidance from the Executive Director for the Campaign (EDC), the Director develops strategies and effectively manages a diverse set of volunteers, communications, and events to meet the Advancement Office's engagement goals involving alumni, parents, community members, volunteers, and donors. With guidance from the Vice President of Institutional Advancement (VPIA), the Director collaborates with other divisions on campus on the development of college publications, including, but not limited to, the Alumni/University Magazine, University Impact Report, President's Annual Report, and a comprehensive divisional communications plan. This position involves regular and extensive interaction with the President's Office, faculty and staff, donors and prospects, community leaders, high-level volunteers, and alumni. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties include but not limited to: Essential: Works with the EDC and the VPIA to establish long-term goals and objectives for alumni and donor relations programs; recommends short- and long-range strategies to support WSU's mission and advancement goals. Develops, implements, and manages annual communication and constituent engagement plans aligned with the institutional Strategic Plan. Supports the implementation and appropriate use of WSU brand guidelines across the Office of Institutional Advancement. Ensures all communications produced by Institutional Advancement comply with University branding standards, editorial guidelines, and applicable digital accessibility requirements. In collaboration with the Director of Alumni Relations and with input from the Executive Director of Institutional Advancement (EDIA), plans and implements a robust annual alumni relations program marketing plan, including social events, talks, and volunteer opportunities that reflect WSU's distinct culture and engage alumni from all backgrounds and life stages. Develops and maintains a comprehensive annual editorial and communications calendar that aligns Institutional Advancement initiatives with the University's strategic priorities and fundraising objectives and oversees the design and distribution of print and digital marketing for Institutional Advancement programs and initiatives. Develops and evaluates communication metrics to measure engagement, audience reach, and the effectiveness of campaigns, publications, and constituent communications, using data to inform future communication strategies. Helps manage and advise on alumni and friends social media channels. Supports event staffing and logistics for Institutional Advancement programs and events as needed. Serves as the convener of a University Magazine working group to create and execute a plan for a new University Magazine. This group should include staff, faculty, students, alumni, and others. Serves as lead writer and content creator for major University publications and Advancement materials, including the President's Report and University Magazine. Writes and edits compelling journalistic stories highlighting benefactors, beneficiaries, donors, students, and alumni for use in publications, newsletters, press releases, correspondence, social media, and marketing to support the Campaign and other Institutional Advancement efforts. Compiles regular constituent correspondence and collaborates across departments to maintain consistent messaging in outreach materials. Collaborates with Donor Relations and Institutional Advancement staff to ensure timely delivery of annual impact reports to donors, serving as lead writer and designer for content and layout. Works with the EDC, EDIA, and Senior Annual Giving Officer to embed student-focused storytelling into donor stewardship through videos, handwritten notes, and personalized outreach. Supports the design and production of materials for the WSU Foundation and fundraising initiatives, including brochures, appeal letters, newsletters, and branded items. Collaborates with Institutional Advancement staff to create and manage digital outreach, advertising, and strategy for donor appeals and community events such as Giving Day and student-centered fundraising efforts. Manages complex communications and project workflows with minimal supervision, ensuring quality and timeliness. Performs other duties and special projects as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree, preferably in Communications, English, Journalism, Public Relations, or a related field. At least three to five years of professional experience creating and leading the execution of an external communications plan, preferably in a college or university setting. Experience managing publications from concept through production, including editorial planning, writing, editing, and publication management. Experience developing executive-level communications, speeches, annual reports, or leadership messaging. Experience leading complex communications or marketing projects involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Effectively manages multiple projects, balances priorities, and meets deadlines. Outstanding oral and written communication skills. Ability to identify story placement opportunities and think strategically about communications. Demonstrated interviewing skills for content development. Competency with digital communications and social media. Additional Information: Salary: Salaries for current Westfield State University employees and individuals currently working for the state of Massachusetts must be calculated individually in accordance with collective bargaining agreements as well as state policies. State job specifications may be found on the Department of Higher Education's webpage . Employee Benefits: Benefits are an important component of an employee's total compensation package. Health Insurance: Westfield State offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: the MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Additional information regarding employee benefits is available on the University's Benefits & Wellness webpage . Disability Accommodations Westfield State University is committed to the full inclusion of individuals with disabilities and will ensure the availability of reasonable accommodations. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at (413) 572-8809 or visit us in the Horace Mann Building, 1st floor. Background Check Employment is contingent upon the successful completion and review of a background check. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify an applicant from consideration. Application Instructions: An on-line application is required. The successful candidate must submit an official transcript at the time of hire. Interested candidates should electronically attach the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Contact information for three references * Copy of unofficial transcript of highest degree * Provide the contact information for reference providers in the reference section of the online application. Deadline: The job posting will be open a minimum of ten days and, if needed, will remain open until finalists have been selected. NOTE: If you need assistance completing your application please contact our online Help Desk . The link to the help desk can be found at the top of the page via Contact Us. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Westfield State University 577 Western Avenue, Westfield,  MA  01086"
    },
    "https://westfield.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203909": {
      "title": "Case Manager",
      "description": "Westfield State University\nJob Posting: Case Manager Westfield State University \n\tJob Posting: Case Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Case Manager Category: Professional/Executive Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: ENROLLMENT MANAGEMENT Locations: Westfield, MA Posted: Aug 19, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $60,000.00 - $63,000.00 Position ID: 203909 Share About Westfield State University: In 1839, Westfield State University was founded on the ideals of Horace Mann who sought to improve society through education. We were the first public education institution without barrier to race, gender or economic class. The spirit of innovative thinking and social responsibility is forged in a curriculum of liberal arts and professional studies contributing to the development of knowledge, skills, and character essential for students to become responsible leaders and engaged citizens. Westfield State is a highly residential campus with approximately 55% of our 3,100 full-time undergraduate students living on campus. The campus is ideally situated on the edge of the Berkshire Mountains in western Massachusetts just 30 minutes from the thriving cultural centers of Springfield, Northampton, and Amherst with a selection of museums, theater, collegiate and minor league sports, hiking trails, and restaurants. The University is within 1.5 hours of Boston and Albany and within 3 hours of New York City and the Green Mountain range of Vermont. Thank You for Your Interest in Becoming a Westfield State Community Member You are welcome here. You can advance your career and make a difference here. We invite you to bring your whole self and talents to Westfield State University. The University seeks applicants whose record of teaching, student advising, research, and administration positions them to contribute to the everyday practice of our institutional values. Our Values Westfield State commits to values that strengthen a common bond among all members of our community and promotes a rich campus environment. Embrace Diversity - We treat all members of our community with dignity and respect. Maintain Excellence and Integrity - We maintain excellence and integrity in all that we do. Collaborate with Each Other - We make decisions in a transparent and collaborative manner. Provide Accessible Education - We commit to providing an accessible, affordable public higher education for all. Build a Strong Community - We are inclusive and ensure equity, supporting the personal development of all community members, and embracing multiple perspectives. Engage the Outside Community - We support civic engagement in local, regional, and global initiatives. Job Description: Campus Title: Case Manager State Job Title: Staff Assistant Department: Enrollment Management Job Code: HA5600 FLSA Status: Exempt Funding: 1596-2439 (Grant Funded)* Bargaining Unit: APA Job Type: Full-Time Temporary / On-campus position Timeframe: 52 Weeks Shift: Monday-Friday, 8:30 am to 4:30 pm (some nights and weekends required) Regular Days Off: Saturday and Sunday Salary: $60,000 to $63,000 Annually (commensurate with education and experience) *This is a grant-funded position. Continued employment beyond the grant period is contingent upon the availability of funding and institutional need. Upon the grant's conclusion, the position will be evaluated for potential adoption and funding by Westfield State University. General Statement of Duties: Under the general direction of the Office of the Dean of Students this position with help to respond to the needs of students (graduate and undergraduate) encountering personal or academic challenges. The University Case Manager collaborates with other offices to develop programs that enhance the quality of student life, promote all facets of well-being, and respond to student concerns. The University Case Manager is expected to be available to staff and students outside regular business hours, for evening and weekend events, and/or at other critical times. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties include but not limited to: Essential: Maintains strong working relationships and collaborations between the Office of the Dean of Students, students, and various University departments. Maintains current knowledge of student needs, including graduate students, student development, and student learning research, theory, and practice that best serve the needs of students. Represents the Office of the Dean of Students at campus-wide functions. Recommends and participates in the development of University policies and procedures. Develops a strong relationship with local hospitals, particularly at the time of the discharge of students. Supports and advocates for students (graduate and undergraduate) experiencing crises; intervenes directly in sensitive cases involving critical illness or injury, mental illness, and fatalities. Contributes to the case management process of the office by meeting with students on sensitive and private issues and provides guidance and support to students and families during times of crisis. In cases where students need extra mental health support or other type of clinical assistance necessary for the retention, persistence, and success of the student, the case manager collaborates, when requested, by the Dean of Students Office, with students, families, campus partners, and off campus resources to form comprehensive plans for student success and assists in the plan implementation. Implements the administrative activities associated with the Office of the Dean of Students to support students, including medical leave of absences and withdrawals. Advises faculty, staff, students, and families in complex problem solving and complaint resolution in situations that pose a risk to students and/or the institution. Consults and engages in problem-solving on complex matters with Residence Life, Counseling Center, Health Center, University Police, Student, Student Accessibility Services, TRiO, Course Achievement Retention and Engagement, LEAD Scholars and Academic Advising. Advises the Office of the Dean of Student staff in best practices related to students that impact case management practices and policies. Collaborates with the student leader trainings and orientation programs. Serves as an advisor for the Office of Student Conduct. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Requirements: QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in social work, higher education, student personnel, counseling services, or other related field and four years of full-time professional experience working with college students. Commitment to the knowledge of multicultural, diversity, and LGBTQ+ issues. Experience with strategizing, planning, and delivering communications. Familiarity with college student learning and development theories. Knowledge of student support programs and services. Experience with outreach initiatives and program development. Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to use independent judgment and manage and impart information to a range of clientele and/or media sources. Effective interpersonal and community relations skills. Ability to build positive and effective relationships with colleagues and student leaders across the University. Skilled in managing crises and knowledge of and experience with crisis intervention techniques. Ability to react calmly and effectively in emergency situations. Ability to take initiative for projects and the development of services. Ability to collaborate and work successfully in a team environment. Experience with case management software, student information system software such as Maxient. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community and rapidly changing technical environment. Additional Information: Salary: Salaries for current Westfield State University employees and individuals currently working for the state of Massachusetts must be calculated individually in accordance with collective bargaining agreements as well as state policies. State job specifications may be found on the Department of Higher Education's webpage . Employee Benefits: Benefits are an important component of an employee's total compensation package. Health Insurance: Westfield State offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: the MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Additional information regarding employee benefits is available on the University's Benefits & Wellness webpage . Disability Accommodations Westfield State University is committed to the full inclusion of individuals with disabilities and will ensure the availability of reasonable accommodations. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at (413) 572-8809 or visit us in the Horace Mann Building, 1st floor. Background Check Employment is contingent upon the successful completion and review of a background check. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify an applicant from